{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>He went up.</b> As it sounds — it was entirely a burnt-offering." "<b>And they sacrificed.</b> Peace-offerings." "<b>And Aharon came, etc.</b> And where did Moshe go? Was it not he who went out to meet him and caused him all that honor? Rather, he was standing and serving before them (Mekhilta)." "<b>Before HaElohim.</b> From here: one who benefits from a meal at which scholars are seated — it is as though he benefited from the radiance of the Shekhinah (Berakhot 64)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:57.776393737Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}